L3afpad @VERSION@ - a simple text editor (GTK 3) for RISC OS

L3afpad 0.8.18.1.11 by Tarot Osuji and Steven Honeyman (GPL version 2),
on GTK 3 through riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend: the first real GTK program
in the riscos-gtk project.

Using it
- Run it: L3afpad puts its icon on the icon bar. Click Select on the icon
  to open a window. Or drop a text file on !L3afpad in a Filer window.
- Each text has its own window, as in Edit: Select on the icon, and
  File > New, open a new empty window; a text file dropped on the icon,
  or double-clicked while L3afpad is loaded, opens in a window of its
  own (a file that's open already has its window brought to the front).
  Running !L3afpad again gives the file to the copy that's running.
- The icon bar icon: Select opens a new window; Menu gives Info (About
  this program), Choices... and Quit.
- Quit (or a desktop shutdown) with unsaved text in any window asks:
  Cancel or Discard. File > Quit asks in each window with unsaved text.
- Closing a window asks to save first; L3afpad stays on the icon bar
  until you choose Quit.
- Choices...: font, tab width, word wrap, line numbers, auto indent. Set
  uses them in every window, and keeps them in
  <Choices$Write>.L3afpad.Choices for new windows.
- Click Menu over the window for its menu (File, Edit, Search, Options,
  Help). Keyboard short-cuts are shown in the menus (^S save, ^O open...).
- Drag a text file from a Filer window onto a window to open it there.
- File > Save As: a RISC OS Save box. Drag its icon to a Filer window, or
  give a full name and click Save. Names without an extension are saved
  as Text (&FFF).
- File > Open: an Open box. Drag a file to it from a Filer window.
- File > Print...: the RISC OS Print box (All or From/to pages, Copies,
  Scale, Upright/Sideways, Draft; Save keeps the settings). It prints to
  the printer set up in !Printers. File > Print Preview shows the pages
  first, with Print to print them.
- Text in UTF-8 and other encodings is detected when opening; RISC OS's
  Latin-1 is read through the Iconv module.

Not yet
- Double-clicking a text file when L3afpad isn't loaded starts your usual
  editor, not L3afpad (it doesn't claim Text files in its !Boot).

Messages go to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.L3afpad.Log. Please send it, with a note of
anything that behaves differently from a RISC OS editor.

Built with riscos-crossdev 1.3 and UnixLib 5.0.3.3.

